---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="What is PCD? — Processing Community Day"
  description="Processing Community Day is a global network of community-led events celebrating creative coding and the open-source tools behind it."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="prose__eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>What is Processing Community Day?</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Processing Community Day is a global network of community-led events that brings together
      artists, designers, technologists, educators, students, and open-source communities around the
      world.
    </p>

    <p>
      It is a chance to share our passion for creative coding, and to celebrate the people and
      communities who create, maintain, teach, and sustain the open-source tools that make it
      possible, including but not limited to <a href="https://processing.org/">Processing</a> and
      <a href="https://p5js.org/">p5.js</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Each event is independently organized by its local community, which means every PCD is
      different and reflects the people and context of that place. What we all share is a love for
      creative coding!
    </p>

    <p>
      There is no single official date for PCD, but we encourage events to take place during October
      so all of us around the world can celebrate together.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Anyone can host a PCD.</strong> If you would like to organize an event in your city,
        the <a href="/organize/">Organizer's Kit</a> walks you through it, from the simplest possible
        version to a full day of workshops and talks.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
